Subject: [PATCH 6.18.y 0/3] can: backport of the per-device receive list lock series

This series backports the following upstream commits to 6.18.y, which
failed to apply to the 6.18-stable tree:

  962947b69589 ("can: replace ARPHRD_CAN type checks with can_get_ml_priv()")
  0f3ad9ab40e3 ("can: protect the receive lists with a per-device lock")
  43c973a0887d ("can: raw, isotp: copy socket options outside of lock_sock()")

They build on each other and have to be applied in this order. This
series answers all three FAILED mails:

  <20261109200450-failed-6.18-962947b69589@kernel.org>
  <20261109200455-failed-6.18-0f3ad9ab40e3@kernel.org>
  <20261109200452-failed-6.18-43c973a0887d@kernel.org>

The adaptations to this tree are described in each patch. The series
applies on top of linux-6.18.y plus the already queued patches

  933bf0fcb325 ("can: isotp: check the frame type, not just the length")
  874f5f14cf62 ("can: isotp: check the return values of can_rx_register() in isotp_bind()")
  12297f855bbd ("can: proc: reset pkg_stats atomics individually")
  01b19ed9fa03 ("can: proc: skip stats calculation after reset in can_stat_update()")

and builds without errors or warnings after each patch.

Oliver Hartkopp (3):
  can: replace ARPHRD_CAN type checks with can_get_ml_priv()
  can: protect the receive lists with a per-device lock
  can: raw, isotp: copy socket options outside of lock_sock()

